# ============================================================
# ResNet-12 (MTL architecture, 160-320-640) + Meta-Transfer Learning (MTL)
# Faithful re-implementation of yaoyao-liu/meta-transfer-learning (PyTorch)
# Controlled resolution ablation — miniImageNet, 84x84 vs 224x224
# Multi-seed (mean +/- std across seeds)
#
# WHAT CHANGED VS THE PROTONET BASELINE SCRIPT:
# This script replaces the "from-scratch ResNet-12 + standard ProtoNet"
# pipeline with the ORIGINAL Meta-Transfer Learning (MTL, CVPR2019)
# method, reproduced as closely as possible from the authors' PyTorch
# code (models/mtl.py, models/conv2d_mtl.py, models/resnet_mtl.py,
# trainer/pre.py, trainer/meta.py):
#
#   1. Backbone: ResNet-12 with channel widths 160-320-640 (NOT
#      64-128-256-512), 3-conv residual blocks with a strided conv in
#      the first conv of each block (no explicit max-pool layer),
#      global average pool -> 640-dim embedding. This exactly matches
#      models/resnet_mtl.py in the original repo.
#
#   2. Conv2dMtl (Scaling & Shifting): every convolution in the
#      backbone has FROZEN original weights (`requires_grad=False`)
#      plus a small learnable per-output-channel scale (`mtl_weight`,
#      init 1) and shift (`mtl_bias`, init 0). Only these SS
#      parameters (and BatchNorm) are trained during meta-training —
#      NOT the frozen conv weights. This is the paper's core idea.
#
#   3. BaseLearner: a single linear layer (640 -> n_way) that is
#      adapted PER-EPISODE via `update_step` manual SGD steps on the
#      support set (MAML-style inner loop), computed with
#      torch.autograd.grad + functional re-application of fast
#      weights — exactly as in models/mtl.py's meta_forward().
#
#   4. Two-phase training, exactly as trainer/pre.py + trainer/meta.py:
#        Stage 1 (pre-train): plain ResNet-12 (no SS, weights NOT
#          frozen) trained as a normal classifier (SGD + momentum +
#          nesterov + weight_decay) over all 64 base classes.
#        Stage 2 (meta-train): SS-ResNet-12 (frozen backbone weights,
#          only SS + BatchNorm trainable) + BaseLearner, initialized
#          from Stage 1's encoder weights, trained episodically with
#          Adam using TWO learning rates (meta_lr1 for encoder SS
#          params, meta_lr2 for the BaseLearner), and the manual
#          inner-loop adaptation described above.
#
# WHAT WAS KEPT FROM THE ORIGINAL BASELINE SCRIPT (infrastructure):
#   - Kaggle/Colab auto-detection, dataset attach/download handling
#   - StageTimer / stage-time summary
#   - FLOPs/params/latency/peak-memory efficiency profiling
#   - Episodic sampler, 84x84 / 224x224 transform variants
#   - Multi-seed aggregation (mean +/- std) and resolution-delta report
#
# NOTE ON RESOLUTION ABLATION FOR THIS BACKBONE:
# Exactly as in the from-scratch baseline, this MTL backbone has NO
# ImageNet-pretrained weights available (no public checkpoint exists
# for this custom architecture), so Stage 1 always starts from random
# initialization here too. The "resolution alignment with ImageNet
# pretraining" argument still does not apply; running 84 vs 224 tests
# whether extra spatial detail helps Stage-1 representation learning
# and, downstream, the quality of the SS + BaseLearner adaptation.
# ============================================================

