# ============================================================
# ResNet-12 Standard ProtoNet — miniImageNet
# Training from scratch, both 84×84 and 224×224
#
# SCIENTIFIC PURPOSE
# ------------------
# This script fills the critical gap in MobileProtoNet's
# comparison table: the FSL literature's actual ResNet-12
# (64-160-320-640 channels, trained from random initialization
# on the FSL base classes) versus MobileProtoNet.
#
# Two conditions are run:
#
#   A) ResNet-12 @ 84×84  (standard FSL protocol)
#      → The "fair" comparison to MetaOptNet, FEAT, SCL, APFP.
#        All those papers train from scratch at 84×84.
#        Expected: ~62–68% (1-shot), matching literature.
#
#   B) ResNet-12 @ 224×224 (resolution-aligned protocol)
#      → Tests whether the resolution alignment benefit
#        also applies to a from-scratch ResNet-12.
#        Expected: higher than A but likely below MobileNetV3
#        @ 224×224, since ResNet-12 lacks ImageNet pretraining.
#        This answers: "does 224×224 help even without pretraining?"
#
# TRAINING PROTOCOL
# -----------------
# From-scratch ResNet-12 training requires a LONGER Stage 1
# than the ImageNet-pretrained experiments (which needed only
# 10 epochs). We use 60 epochs for Stage 1, matching the
# typical schedule in FSL literature papers (MetaOptNet uses
# 60 epochs, FEAT uses 100). Stage 2 follows the same episodic
# curriculum as all prior experiments (Adam lr=1e-5, 1000 eps).
#
# ARCHITECTURE
# ------------
# Standard FSL ResNet-12 (Oreshkin et al. 2018 / Lee et al. 2019):
#   4 residual blocks with channel widths [64, 160, 320, 640]
#   Each block: [Conv-BN-LeakyReLU] × 3 + MaxPool + residual shortcut
#   Output: 640-dim embedding after global average pooling
#
# WHAT TO REPORT IN THE PAPER
# ----------------------------
# After running this script, add two rows to Table 3:
#
#   ResNet-12 + Std ProtoNet  |  84×84  |  0 (no ImageNet)  |  XX.XX%  |  YY.YY%
#   ResNet-12 + Std ProtoNet  |  224×224 |  0 (no ImageNet)  |  XX.XX%  |  YY.YY%
#
# This lets reviewers see:
#   1. Our method vs ResNet-12 at matched 84×84 protocol
#   2. Whether resolution alignment helps ResNet-12 too
#   3. The importance of ImageNet pretraining vs resolution alone
# ============================================================

# ============================================
# 0. INSTALL & IMPORTS
# ============================================
